- Omarchy. Copyright David Heinemeier Hansson / Basecamp.
  https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy

SMF Works authored SMF Praxis and SMF Swarm 2.0, both MIT. Praxis Prime is a
new codebase. This skeleton does not vendor their source trees.

Third-party material that is copied in later must keep its original copyright
header, license, and NOTICE. The inventory, including Apache-2.0 files whose
notices have to travel with the code, is in THIRD_PARTY.md (also referred to
from the architecture blueprint as THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

The six public MIT regulated packs (homeschool, education, forensic, legal,
medical, behavioral health) ship as data under packs/regulated/. Each pack
directory keeps its LICENSE and NOTICE. Their Python modules and dashboard
JavaScript are not included. Compliance dials stay off until an admin turns
one on. Versions of that code released under MIT before Praxis 0.29.0 stay MIT
for the people who received them. Any further private pack repository is still
out of this tree. See packs/regulated/README.md and THIRD_PARTY.md.

This software is not a certification of HIPAA, FERPA, GDPR, or any other
regime. The compliance dials are off by default and, in this pre-alpha
skeleton, do not enforce anything.
